observations.management_comment:
5.20. The DOA committed to comply with the recommendations on issues raised. They have already coordinated with the relevant offices and bureaus of the City to promptly act on the recommendations.

5.21. On the other hand, the CTO has been implementing the following measures in order to intensify RPT Collections:

Issuance of NODs to different barangays from all districts which revealed various delinquencies since CY 2020;

The CTO shall issue the corresponding warrant of levy as soon as it has determined the delinquent properties that shall be subjected to auction;

CTO shall exert effort to furnish all barangays on the existence of each delinquent properties; and

The CTO shall also furnish the city council of all NODs sent to each barangays and shall post on conspicuous places of all districts all delinquent properties.

commendations.text:
The Office of the City Accountant (OCAT), during the year, immediately effected the following adjustments to various accounts in the financial statements (FS):
a. Property, Plant and Equipment (PPE) accounts amounting to P14.259 million were adjusted to correct the inappropriate recording of the unserviceable and disposed PPE;
b. PPE accounts amounting to P1.101 billion were reverted back to their appropriate accounts to correct the erroneous recording of year-end adjustments;
c. The set-up of obligations amounting to P23.924 million and errors in the posting of payments amounting to P8.841 million were already corrected; and
d. The particulars in some payable transactions amounting to P141.822 million were already provided.

The Management addressed the issues raised on the following:
a. Submission of documentary requirements for the 21 sampled Disbursement Vouchers (DVs) totaling P755.609 million;
b. Submission of Purchase Orders, Notices of Delivery, and Inspection and Acceptance Reports;
c. Issues with the machine errors in the printing of checks were already addressed; and
d. The information and publicity of PPAs, and reporting requirements provided under Section 28, Article II of the 1987 Philippine Constitution and COA Circular No. 2013-004 dated January 30, 2013, as amended, were complied with.
